#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:100
msgid "Client portal path"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:101
msgid "The path of the client portal on your Profotograaf address, used by the \"Find your gallery\" block. A block can set its own. The default is /client."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:108
msgid "Use Profotograaf photos in the editor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:109
msgid "Lets editors who can upload files browse your Profotograaf photos in the block editor and add them to the Media Library. While this is on, the site asks Profotograaf for your photo list and downloads the photos an editor picks, and editors' browsers load thumbnails from profotograaf.nl. A photo an editor uses is stored on this site. Only galleries with embedding switched on are offered. While this is off, nothing is requested."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:115
msgid "Keep photos on Profotograaf"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:116
msgid "Adds the choice \"Keep on Profotograaf\" next to Import on the Import from Profotograaf screen, for editors who can upload files. A photo kept on Profotograaf is added to the Media Library without a download. This site shows it from Profotograaf and stores no copy. It needs \"Use Profotograaf photos in the editor\". If you unpublish a gallery on Profotograaf, its photos stop loading from Profotograaf at once, but copies already held by edge caches and by visitors' browsers can keep showing for up to a year. Import the photos you may want to withdraw later. If you switch this off, the photos kept on Profotograaf stop showing on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:122
msgid "Send Media Library files to Profotograaf"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:123
msgid "Lets editors who can upload files send images to a Profotograaf gallery you link below. A file is sent only after a person chooses a linked gallery for it, in the attachment details, with the bulk action in the Media Library list, or automatically for a gallery where you switch that on. The original image goes to Profotograaf with its EXIF data except the GPS position, which is removed first. Later changes to the title, caption and alt text of a sent file are sent too. Files are sent in the background, never while you save."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:129
msgid "Default gallery layout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:130
msgid "Used when a gallery block or shortcode does not choose a layout. Profotograaf default shows each gallery in the closest layout your site can draw: grid, masonry or slideshow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:142
msgid "Collect enquiries"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:143
msgid "Listen for submissions of supported form plugins. Each form still has its own switch on the enquiry forms screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:149
msgid "Failure alerts go to"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:150
msgid "Receives one email, without personal data, when an enquiry cannot be delivered or is dropped. Leave empty to use the site admin email address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:157
msgid "Mail undeliverable enquiries to"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:158
msgid "When an enquiry cannot be delivered to Profotograaf, send it by email to this address instead. The email contains the enquiry. Until you save a choice this is the site admin email address. Save it empty to turn this off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:167
msgid "Keep undeliverable enquiries for (days)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings-schema.php:168
