#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:230
msgid "Pages that show a Profotograaf gallery make the visitor's browser load a script, the gallery data and the photos from profotograaf.nl, a service operated by the plugin author. Profotograaf receives the visitor's IP address and browser details, as any web server does. When a gallery scrolls into view the script reports one anonymous view, with the gallery and the host name of this site. No view is reported when the browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control. The plugin sets no cookies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:231
msgid "Enquiries"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:232
msgid "When a contact form is switched on for Profotograaf, each submission is stored on this site and then sent to profotograaf.nl: the name, email address, phone number, date, message and other fields of the form, the address of the page and the name of the form. A submission waits in the queue until it is delivered. One that cannot be delivered is kept for a limited time, so the site owner can export or retry it. The personal data tools export and erase these submissions by the email address of the sender."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:233
msgid "Photo library in the editor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:234
msgid "Only when the site owner turns on the media source: editors who can upload files can browse the photos of the connected Profotograaf account in the block editor. The site asks profotograaf.nl for the photo list and fetches the photos an editor picks. The editor's browser loads the thumbnails from profotograaf.nl, which receives that editor's IP address and browser details. A photo an editor uses is stored in the Media Library of this site and stays there until it is deleted. To flag changes made on Profotograaf, the copy keeps a sync state, hashes of the file and text as they were written, and the id of the user who kept it or stopped watching it, with the time. No visitor data is involved."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:235
msgid "Sending Media Library files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:236
msgid "Only when the site owner turns on sending Media Library files: a person who can upload files chooses a linked Profotograaf gallery for an image, and this site then sends that image to profotograaf.nl in the background. The gallery can be a client gallery. Before an image is sent, the plugin removes the GPS position from it. The other metadata stays in the file, such as camera, lens and date. Later changes to the title, caption and alt text of a sent image are sent too. HEIC, video and RAW files are not sent. Photos of people are personal data, so the site owner needs a basis for sending them. Deleting a file here deletes nothing on Profotograaf. The Media Library keeps a few hidden fields per sent file (the photo and gallery identifiers, the send state and the time) until the file is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:238
msgid "Only when the site owner switches on copying: this site copies files from its Media Library to the connected Profotograaf account, in the background. It sends the image files, and RAW and video files, with their file names and the access token to https://profotograaf.nl/api/v1/embed/galleries/<gallery id>/photos. It first creates private galleries with https://profotograaf.nl/api/v1/embed/galleries, with the site title in the gallery name. Files are sent as stored, with their metadata, which can include the GPS position. Photos of people are personal data, so the site owner needs a basis for sending them, and Profotograaf stores the copies for the site owner. The anonymous usage data and photo library choices do not switch copying on. Deleting a file here, switching copying off or deleting the plugin leaves the copies in the Profotograaf account until they are deleted there. The Media Library keeps a few hidden fields per file (the copy state, the photo and gallery identifiers and a checksum) until the plugin is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:239
msgid "Connection and diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:240
msgid "When the site owner connects the site, the plugin sends the site title, the site address, the site language, the email address of the site administrator, the plugin version and a random identifier of this installation to profotograaf.nl. Profotograaf uses the site title and administrator email address only to prefill the account sign-up form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:241
msgid "Only when the site owner opts in to anonymous usage data, the plugin sends a daily usage report and reports of its own errors to services operated by the plugin author. They hold the plugin, WordPress and PHP versions, the site language, the active plugin modules, counts of failed connections and enquiry deliveries, and error codes. They hold no site address, visitor data, enquiries or tokens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/class-privacy.php:242
msgid "The Profotograaf privacy policy is at https://profotograaf.nl/privacy."
msgstr ""

